cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ATC Decision-Support Prototype: a specialist-detector architecture for air traffic conflict alerting"
message: "If you use this software or its analysis scripts, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Filipe
    family-names: Brito Ferreira
    email: me@fbritoferreira.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-0200-9417"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-09-02"

repository-code: "https://github.com/fbritoferreira/atc-decision-support"
abstract: >-
  A research prototype testing whether air traffic control conflict alerting can
  be composed from a population of small, independent, deterministic detectors
  sharing a SimState to Alert contract, rather than from a single monolithic rule
  function. Eleven detectors run behind one orchestrator. Includes 28 scenarios:
  9 incidents reconstructed from NTSB, ICAO, CIAIAC and ANSV reports, 11
  negative controls encoding events that resolved safely, three of them from
  specific NASA ASRS reports, and 8 operational demonstrations loaded from the
  application's scenario picker. Ships a monolithic reimplementation of the same
  doctrine for architectural comparison, a live mode ingesting ADS-B and METAR
  for seventeen airports of which ten are in the United States, and the analysis
  scripts behind the reported false-positive sampling. The measurement windows
  themselves are not distributed, so those scripts re-run on a window the user
  samples rather than reproducing the published figures. The software is a
  prototype and is not certified or usable for operational air traffic
  control.
keywords:
  - air-traffic-control
  - decision-support
  - conflict-detection
  - aviation-safety
  - deterministic-systems
  - ADS-B
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the latest version. The
# version-specific DOI for the first deposit is 10.5281/zenodo.22245226;
# cite the concept DOI instead, so a citation does not pin a reader to a
# snapshot that a later release supersedes.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22245225
